direction: down
title: CPU Cache Line Locality & Pointer Traversal Topologies

MemoryLayout: 1. CPU Cache Line Memory Locality {
  A0: "Array[0] (0x00)"
  A1: "Array[1] (0x08)"
  A2: "Array[2] (0x10)"
  A3: "Array[3] (0x18)"
  A4: "Array[4] (0x20)"
  A5: "Array[5] (0x28)"
  A6: "Array[6] (0x30)"
  A7: "Array[7] (0x38)"
  A0 -> A1 -> A2 -> A3 -> A4 -> A5 -> A6 -> A7
}

PointerPatterns: 2. Canonical Pointer Scanning Topologies {
  Convergent: Two Pointers Convergent Scan (L -> <- R)
  Cycle: Fast & Slow Floyd Tortoise & Hare (1x vs 2x)
  SlidingWindow: Dynamic Sliding Window (Expand / Contract)
}

MemoryLayout -> PointerPatterns: Spatial Locality enables O(1) auxiliary scans
